{"actor_id":null,"event_id":"gaia-5d0080cb:tool:0","kind":"tool_call","parent_event_id":null,"payload":{"tool_call":{"app_name":"web_search","arguments":{"max_results":5,"query":"Can Hiccup Supply Enough Fish to Maintain a Dragon's Diet University of Leicester volume fish bag"},"duration_ms":1724.7967720031738,"error":null,"name":"web_search","operation_id":"web_search","result":"1. Can Hiccup Supply Enough Fish to Maintain a Dragon's Diet?\n   URL: https://journals.le.ac.uk/index.php/jist/article/view/733\n   This paper investigates the feasibility of Hiccup, a teenage boy, being able to supply enough fish to maintain the dragon's diet by catching and bringing fish to him. It was found that in the twelve days that Toothless was trapped, he would have required 13 Icelandic cod and 56 Atlantic salmon every day, which totalled 716 kg.\n2. harbor-datasets/datasets/gaia/5d0080cb-90d7-4712-bc33 ... - GitHub\n   URL: https://github.com/harbor-framework/harbor-datasets/blob/main/datasets/gaia/5d0080cb-90d7-4712-bc33-848150e917d3/instruction.md\n   What was the volume in m^3 of the fish bag that was calculated in the University of Leicester paper \"Can Hiccup Supply Enough Fish to Maintain a Dragon's Diet?\"\n3. WebVoyager/data/GAIA_web.jsonl at main - GitHub\n   URL: https://github.com/MinorJerry/WebVoyager/blob/main/data/GAIA_web.jsonl\n   ... volume in m^3 of the fish bag that was calculated in the University of Leicester paper \\\"Can Hiccup Supply Enough Fish to Maintain a Dragon\\u2019s Diet?\\\"\"}.\n4. Vol. 6 (2017) | Journal of Interdisciplinary Science Topics\n   URL: https://journals.le.ac.uk/index.php/jist/issue/view/107\n   This undergraduate module ran from January 2017 to March 2017; papers became visible between these dates as they are accepted by the student Editorial Board. Contributing authors were drawn from University of Leicester 'Natural Science' (UK), McMaster University 'Integrated Science' (Canada) and Universite Paris Descartes 'Centre de Recherches Interdisciplinaires' (France) students. Published ...\n5. Fish. - Semantic Scholar\n   URL: https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/Fish.-Amanpour-Guclu/bc802b67cca37cce9320e90a5a6be9eb15b19c0f\n   Can Hiccup Supply Enough Fish to Maintain a Dragon's Diet? Amal Doua Environmental Science 2017","timestamp":"2026-08-18T19:52:20.078593"}},"sequence":83,"timestamp":null}
{"actor_id":null,"event_id":"gaia-5d0080cb:tool:1","kind":"tool_call","parent_event_id":null,"payload":{"tool_call":{"app_name":"web_fetch","arguments":{"max_chars":12000,"url":"https://journals.le.ac.uk/index.php/jist/article/view/733"},"duration_ms":3436.174154281616,"error":null,"name":"web_fetch","operation_id":"web_fetch","result":"HTTP 200\nURL: https://journals.le.ac.uk/index.php/jist/article/view/733\n\nCan Hiccup Supply Enough Fish to Maintain a Dragon’s Diet? | Journal of Interdisciplinary Science Topics Skip to main content Skip to main navigation menu Skip to site footer Open Menu Journal of Interdisciplinary Science Topics Current Archives About About the Journal Submissions Editorial Team Privacy Statement Contact Search Search Login Home / Archives / Vol. 6 (2017) / Articles Can Hiccup Supply Enough Fish to Maintain a Dragon’s Diet? Authors Amal Doua The Centre for Interdisciplinary Science, University of Leicester Keywords: Film, Biology, Nutrition, Dragon, Toothless, How to Train Your Dragon Abstract Toothless is a Night Fury dragon who appears in the How to Train Your Dragon (HTTYD) franchise, and is said to be the rarest, fastest, and most intelligent of the dragon species. In the 2010 film, Toothless is struck down during a dragon raid and loses his left tail-fin, leaving him trapped in a sunken area. This paper investigates the feasibility of Hiccup, a teenage boy, being able to supply enough fish to maintain the dragon’s diet by catching and bringing fish to him. It was found that in the twelve days that Toothless was trapped, he would have required 13 Icelandic cod and 56 Atlantic salmon every day, which totalled 716 kg. Hiccup would have had to carry 828 fish weighing at total of 8592 kg over the twelve days, which is unrealistic since he struggles to lift a shield in combat. References How to Train Your Dragon Wikia (2017) Toothless (Franchise), 8 March 2017. [Online]. Available at: http://howtotrainyourdragon.wikia.com/wiki/Toothless_(Franchise) . [Accessed 10 March 2017]. How to Train Your Dragon Wikia (2017) Night Fury, 7 March 2017. [Online]. Available at: http://howtotrainyourdragon.wikia.com/wiki/Night_Fury . [Accessed 17 March 2017]. School of Dragons (2014) The Cove. [Online]. Available at: http://www.schoolofdragons.com/how-to-train-your-dragon/areas/the-cove . [Accessed 16 March 2017]. How to Train Your Dragon Wikia (2016) Fish, 11 December 2016. [Online]. Available at: http://howtotrainyourdragon.wikia.com/wiki/Fish . [Accessed 16 March 2017]. Sanders, C. &amp; DeBlois, B. (2010) How To Train Your Dragon. [Film]. United States of America: DreamWorks Animation. Endy (2013) So regarding Hiccup's height - An analysis by a man of science, 2013. [Online]. Available at: http://thatendyperson.tumblr.com/post/55555820720/so-regarding-hiccups-height-an-analysis-by-a . [Accessed 17 March 2017]. idrawdigital (2009) Drawing Tutorial: Anatomy and Proportion #1, 14 January 2009. [Online]. Available at: http://www.idrawdigital.com/2009/01/drawing-tutorial-anatomy-and-proportion-1/ . [Accessed 17 March 2017]. NOAA Fisheries (2016) Atlantic salmon (Salmo salar), 10 February 2016. [Online]. Available at: http://www.nmfs.noaa.gov/pr/species/fish/atlantic-salmon.html . [Accessed 16 March 2017]. Icelandic Seafood International (2013) Icelandic Cod. [Online]. Available at: http://www.icelandseafood.is/responsibility/main-species-fact-sheets-2/icelandic-cod-2/ . [Accessed 16 March 2017]. Wilmot, C. (2005) Gadus morhua (On-line), Animal Diversity Web. [Online]. Available at: http://animaldiversity.org/accounts/Gadus_morhua/ . [Accessed 17 March 2017]. Downloads PDF How to Cite Doua, A. (2017). Can Hiccup Supply Enough Fish to Maintain a Dragon’s Diet?. Journal of Interdisciplinary Science Topics , 6 . Retrieved from https://journals.le.ac.uk/index.php/jist/article/view/733 More Citation Formats ACM ACS APA ABNT Chicago Harvard IEEE MLA Turabian Vancouver Download Citation Endnote/Zotero/Mendeley (RIS) BibTeX Issue 